WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.258 --> 00:00:01.917
- Good morning Believe Nation, it's Evan.

00:00:01.917 --> 00:00:04.391
My one word is "Believe,"
and I believe that you

00:00:04.391 --> 00:00:06.900
have something special,
that when you unleash it,

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:08.865
it will be able to change the world.

00:00:08.865 --> 00:00:11.088
So to help you on your
journey, today's message is,

00:00:11.088 --> 00:00:13.467
stop doing the wrong things.

00:00:13.467 --> 00:00:15.771
Over to you, Jordan B. Peterson.

00:00:15.771 --> 00:00:17.761
(rooster crowing)

00:00:17.761 --> 00:00:20.500
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:23.376
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:00:23.376 --> 00:00:26.876
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:28.563 --> 00:00:32.454
- Stop doing the things
that you know are wrong,

00:00:32.454 --> 00:00:35.087
that you could stop doing.

00:00:35.087 --> 00:00:37.851
Right, so it's a fairly limited attempt,

00:00:37.851 --> 00:00:40.174
first of all, we're not
going to say that you know

00:00:40.174 --> 00:00:42.002
what the good is, or what the truth is,

00:00:42.002 --> 00:00:43.714
in any ultimate sense.

00:00:43.714 --> 00:00:45.471
But we will presume that there are things

00:00:45.471 --> 00:00:47.055
that you're doing, that
for one reason or other,

00:00:47.055 --> 00:00:48.881
you know are not in your best interests.

00:00:48.881 --> 00:00:50.083
There's something about them,

00:00:50.083 --> 00:00:51.948
that you just know you should stop.

00:00:51.948 --> 00:00:53.915
They're kind of self-evident to you.

00:00:53.915 --> 00:00:55.754
Other things you're going
to be doubtful about.

00:00:55.754 --> 00:00:57.777
You're not going to know which way is up,

00:00:57.777 --> 00:01:00.323
and which way is down.

00:01:00.323 --> 00:01:01.411
But there are things that you're doing,

00:01:01.411 --> 00:01:03.100
that you know you shouldn't do.

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:05.494
Now, some of those you won't stop doing.

00:01:05.494 --> 00:01:07.255
For whatever reason, you
don't have the discipline,

00:01:07.255 --> 00:01:09.307
or maybe there's a secondary payoff, or,

00:01:09.307 --> 00:01:10.910
you don't believe it's
necessary, or it's too much

00:01:10.910 --> 00:01:12.795
of a sacrifice, or, you're angry,

00:01:12.795 --> 00:01:15.596
or, resentful, or, afraid, who knows.

00:01:15.596 --> 00:01:17.859
So forget about those for now.

00:01:17.859 --> 00:01:20.753
But there's another subset
that you could stop doing.

00:01:20.753 --> 00:01:22.023
It might be a little thing.

00:01:22.023 --> 00:01:24.339
Well, that's fine, stop doing it.

00:01:24.339 --> 00:01:25.673
And see what happens.

00:01:25.673 --> 00:01:29.480
And what'll happen is, your
vision will clear a little bit.

00:01:29.480 --> 00:01:32.277
And then, something else
will pop up, in your field

00:01:32.277 --> 00:01:35.043
of apprehension, that you
will also know you should

00:01:35.043 --> 00:01:37.514
stop doing, and that you could stop doing.

00:01:37.514 --> 00:01:39.005
Cause you strengthened yourself a bit,

00:01:39.005 --> 00:01:40.883
by stopping doing the
particular stupid thing

00:01:40.883 --> 00:01:42.140
that you were doing before.

00:01:42.140 --> 00:01:44.265
That just puts you
together a little bit more.

00:01:44.265 --> 00:01:47.220
And you could do that repeatedly,

00:01:47.220 --> 00:01:49.563
for an indefinite period of time.

00:01:49.563 --> 00:01:52.547
And, you know, that doesn't
necessarily mean that

00:01:52.547 --> 00:01:55.612
you're going to ever be
able to formulate a clear,

00:01:55.612 --> 00:01:58.480
and final picture of what
constitutes the truth,

00:01:58.480 --> 00:02:00.678
and the good, but it does mean, that,

00:02:00.678 --> 00:02:02.564
you'll be able to continually move away

00:02:02.564 --> 00:02:05.462
from what's untruth, and what's bad.

00:02:05.462 --> 00:02:07.736
And, you know, that's not a bad start.

00:02:07.736 --> 00:02:08.569
(whoosh sound effect)

00:02:08.569 --> 00:02:10.094
- So I love the message of
stop doing the wrong things.

00:02:10.094 --> 00:02:11.635
I think it's vitally important,

00:02:11.635 --> 00:02:13.853
the question then becomes, how?

00:02:13.853 --> 00:02:15.733
And if we're eliminating the
things that Jordan Peterson

00:02:15.733 --> 00:02:18.510
said are giving us some kind
of benefit, then the ones

00:02:18.510 --> 00:02:20.536
that are left, at least in
my opinion, are the ones

00:02:20.536 --> 00:02:22.317
that are giving you fear.

00:02:22.317 --> 00:02:24.375
The ones that you are afraid
of doing, and so that you

00:02:24.375 --> 00:02:26.811
don't go out and do it,
or the fear is making you

00:02:26.811 --> 00:02:28.462
continue to do it.

00:02:28.462 --> 00:02:31.078
And so for me, whenever
there's been that kind of fear,

00:02:31.078 --> 00:02:33.142
I'm doing something, or
I'm not doing something

00:02:33.142 --> 00:02:36.809
out of fear, the solution
has always been to create

00:02:36.809 --> 00:02:40.894
a bigger fear in the future,
and bring it back to today.

00:02:40.894 --> 00:02:43.791
It's not, pretend like
the fear doesn't exist.

00:02:43.791 --> 00:02:45.574
It's not, pretend like
that big scary thing

00:02:45.574 --> 00:02:48.597
that you have to go and do, isn't real,

00:02:48.597 --> 00:02:51.324
it's just, I make the
future fear a lot bigger

00:02:51.324 --> 00:02:52.562
than the current fear.

00:02:52.562 --> 00:02:53.708
And so think about that thing

00:02:53.708 --> 00:02:54.766
that you wish you can go and do.

00:02:54.766 --> 00:02:56.986
Think about that project that
you really want to start,

00:02:56.986 --> 00:02:58.496
or that person that you
really want to talk to,

00:02:58.496 --> 00:02:59.784
that connection you really want to make.

00:02:59.784 --> 00:03:02.118
Whatever the thing is, that's
kind of gnawing at you,

00:03:02.118 --> 00:03:04.158
that you really really
really want to go out and do.

00:03:04.158 --> 00:03:07.278
But you're not, because you're afraid.

00:03:07.278 --> 00:03:09.291
Think about your life, you know,

00:03:09.291 --> 00:03:12.055
when you're 80, 90, you
know, 200 years old.

00:03:12.055 --> 00:03:15.051
And then, look back on this moment.

00:03:15.051 --> 00:03:18.026
And the fact that you did
not take action on it,

00:03:18.026 --> 00:03:21.693
has now lead to a life
of decades of regret.

00:03:22.883 --> 00:03:25.649
And I try to make that
as painful as possible.

00:03:25.649 --> 00:03:28.226
As real and painful as possible.

00:03:28.226 --> 00:03:31.091
And bring that back to right now, so that,

00:03:31.091 --> 00:03:33.900
I'm so afraid of the future fear,

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:35.728
that I have to go and take action.

00:03:35.728 --> 00:03:37.322
And it doesn't mean that always works out.

00:03:37.322 --> 00:03:38.925
A lot of times it may
not work out, you know.

00:03:38.925 --> 00:03:41.868
You may get rejected,
that deal may not work.

00:03:41.868 --> 00:03:43.956
You know, you may lose money on something.

00:03:43.956 --> 00:03:47.016
But for me, knowing is the key.

00:03:47.016 --> 00:03:48.659
I can deal with failure.

00:03:48.659 --> 00:03:50.102
I can deal with something not working out.

00:03:50.102 --> 00:03:52.396
Hopefully I don't make it
a huge, colossal failure.

00:03:52.396 --> 00:03:54.200
I could deal with the failure, but what

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:56.500
I can't deal with, is not knowing.

00:03:56.500 --> 00:03:58.391
And so two quick examples
I want to share with you.

00:03:58.391 --> 00:04:00.379
One, there was this
event called Climber Con

00:04:00.379 --> 00:04:02.776
in California, earlier this year,

00:04:02.776 --> 00:04:04.658
and I hate going to events
where I'm not speaking,

00:04:04.658 --> 00:04:06.311
I don't like networking,
I don't like going

00:04:06.311 --> 00:04:07.886
to conferences, it's just not something

00:04:07.886 --> 00:04:09.247
that I enjoy doing.

00:04:09.247 --> 00:04:12.031
But it was for YouTubers with
100,000 plus subscribers,

00:04:12.031 --> 00:04:14.786
and some of the people
that I knew were going,

00:04:14.786 --> 00:04:16.758
that I had kind of met
virtually, and I thought,

00:04:16.758 --> 00:04:20.042
this might be something
that I should go to.

00:04:20.042 --> 00:04:23.209
For once, an event looked interesting,

00:04:24.212 --> 00:04:26.222
for me to go to as a participant,

00:04:26.222 --> 00:04:27.964
and not as a speaker.

00:04:27.964 --> 00:04:30.230
And I was hemming and hawing,
like, ah, should I go,

00:04:30.230 --> 00:04:32.417
should I not go, and I delayed really long

00:04:32.417 --> 00:04:34.554
before, I eventually buy
my ticket, and I just

00:04:34.554 --> 00:04:38.171
came to the point where, I'm
going to regret not going.

00:04:38.171 --> 00:04:40.057
I can deal with it not working
out, I can deal with it

00:04:40.057 --> 00:04:43.433
being a total bust, meeting
nobody, making no connections,

00:04:43.433 --> 00:04:45.699
wasting my time, wasting my money to go,

00:04:45.699 --> 00:04:47.525
I could deal with that, and if anything,

00:04:47.525 --> 00:04:50.114
it would prove my point
that networking events suck,

00:04:50.114 --> 00:04:52.759
and I'm never going to
go to another one again.

00:04:52.759 --> 00:04:53.907
But I needed to know.

00:04:53.907 --> 00:04:55.604
And so I booked my ticket, and I went,

00:04:55.604 --> 00:04:57.158
and it was okay.

00:04:57.158 --> 00:04:59.555
You know, I probably just
got my money's worth.

00:04:59.555 --> 00:05:02.445
It wasn't amazing, it wasn't
some huge success story,

00:05:02.445 --> 00:05:05.480
but I made some new connections,
I got to go face to face

00:05:05.480 --> 00:05:08.563
with some people that
I had met before, and,

00:05:08.563 --> 00:05:09.781
I learned a couple of things.

00:05:09.781 --> 00:05:13.377
So it was not, a little
bit positive, right.

00:05:13.377 --> 00:05:16.201
Another example, when I
was promoting my book,

00:05:16.201 --> 00:05:18.137
I worked with a number of
different people to help me

00:05:18.137 --> 00:05:21.324
promote it, different agencies,
different connections,

00:05:21.324 --> 00:05:23.602
and there was one, who,

00:05:23.602 --> 00:05:26.888
had a reputation that
looked really interesting,

00:05:26.888 --> 00:05:28.479
and gave me a proposal,

00:05:28.479 --> 00:05:32.039
and, I was a little
skeptical of doing it, but,

00:05:32.039 --> 00:05:33.992
again, I felt like

00:05:33.992 --> 00:05:37.171
if I didn't say yes, I would regret it.

00:05:37.171 --> 00:05:38.754
And so, I said yes.

00:05:39.601 --> 00:05:42.296
And, to be honest, it
didn't really work out.

00:05:42.296 --> 00:05:44.114
You know, I paid a lot of money.

00:05:44.114 --> 00:05:46.760
I didn't get, I didn't get the result.

00:05:46.760 --> 00:05:49.098
I didn't get my money's worth at all.

00:05:49.098 --> 00:05:51.191
I didn't get zero value,
but I didn't get the value

00:05:51.191 --> 00:05:54.059
that I felt I had paid for.

00:05:54.059 --> 00:05:55.203
But it's okay.

00:05:55.203 --> 00:05:58.076
Like, it's a lesson learned,
and I'm not going to live

00:05:58.076 --> 00:06:01.412
the next 90 years with regret, that,

00:06:01.412 --> 00:06:02.964
I didn't say yes, and you're wondering,

00:06:02.964 --> 00:06:05.692
what if, what if, what
if, what if, what if.

00:06:05.692 --> 00:06:07.451
You know, there's been other
times where it has worked out,

00:06:07.451 --> 00:06:09.988
insanely well, when I
worked with my agent,

00:06:09.988 --> 00:06:12.210
for the first time, I
almost didn't say yes.

00:06:12.210 --> 00:06:14.150
I was on the fence, and I just felt like

00:06:14.150 --> 00:06:15.960
I might regret it, and it worked out

00:06:15.960 --> 00:06:17.261
really really really well.

00:06:17.261 --> 00:06:19.637
I got a lot better on camera.

00:06:19.637 --> 00:06:21.366
My YouTube channel started to explode.

00:06:21.366 --> 00:06:23.447
I got a book deal, and
other opportunities.

00:06:23.447 --> 00:06:27.114
And so, don't be so
attached to the outcome,

00:06:27.973 --> 00:06:30.237
of it working or not working, right.

00:06:30.237 --> 00:06:32.560
Like it has to work, or
it was a huge failure.

00:06:32.560 --> 00:06:34.706
For me, it's much more, if
there's something that I

00:06:34.706 --> 00:06:37.576
feel like I might regret,

00:06:37.576 --> 00:06:40.327
and you're just delaying
and delaying and delaying,

00:06:40.327 --> 00:06:42.005
eventually, that window's going to close,

00:06:42.005 --> 00:06:43.704
you're going to miss your opportunity.

00:06:43.704 --> 00:06:47.504
And so, make that future fear so big,

00:06:47.504 --> 00:06:48.960
bring it back to today, and say,

00:06:48.960 --> 00:06:53.096
I'm going to regret this for
the next 90 years of my life,

00:06:53.096 --> 00:06:54.730
I need to know.

00:06:54.730 --> 00:06:56.557
You could deal with it not
working out, you could deal

00:06:56.557 --> 00:06:58.780
with failure, you could
deal with the rejection,

00:06:58.780 --> 00:07:02.448
but what you can't deal
with, is not knowing.

00:07:02.448 --> 00:07:04.317
So the question today, I'm curious,

00:07:04.317 --> 00:07:06.541
what is that thing that's gnawing at you,

00:07:06.541 --> 00:07:08.855
that you really want to try,
you really want to test,

00:07:08.855 --> 00:07:11.205
you really want to go out
and do, but you're afraid.

00:07:11.205 --> 00:07:13.917
What is that thing for you
right now, in your business,

00:07:13.917 --> 00:07:16.448
in your life, leave it
down in the comments below.

00:07:16.448 --> 00:07:17.895
I'm really curious to find out.

00:07:17.895 --> 00:07:19.903
I also want to give a quick
shout-out to Wim Winters.

00:07:19.903 --> 00:07:22.147
Wim, thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:07:22.147 --> 00:07:24.524
"Your One Word," I really
appreciate the support,

00:07:24.524 --> 00:07:26.294
and I hope you enjoy the read.

00:07:26.294 --> 00:07:28.782
So thank you guys again for
watching, I believe in you,

00:07:28.782 --> 00:07:30.705
I hope you continue to
believe in yourself,

00:07:30.705 --> 00:07:32.772
and whatever your one word is.

00:07:32.772 --> 00:07:35.550
Much love, and I'll see you
guys again tomorrow morning,

00:07:35.550 --> 00:07:38.221
for another shot of Entspresso.

00:07:38.221 --> 00:07:40.906
♫ I wake up every morning

00:07:40.906 --> 00:07:44.889
♫ Espresso keep me going

